# Collectee — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Every value here is a PLACEHOLDER; there are no
# real credentials in this file and none may ever be committed to it.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored (this file is the one exception), so a real
# key cannot be committed by accident. Verify with:
#
#     git check-ignore -v .env
#
# THE APP RUNS WITH NONE OF THESE SET. Nothing below is required to start it,
# browse it or demo it — each one only turns something on. What you lose without
# each is written under it.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never prefix this with EXPO_PUBLIC_.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Anthropic key used by the serverless proxy in `api/assistant.ts`. It is
# read at request time on the server (`process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) and is
# never sent to the client.
#
# ⚠️ This belongs in your Vercel project's environment variables, NOT in a local
# `.env` you bundle. Any variable named `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` is inlined into the
# shipped JavaScript and readable by anyone with the app — putting a billed key
# behind that prefix publishes it. The prefix is the whole difference; the name
# below is deliberately without it.
#
# WITHOUT IT: the proxy returns an error for every model call and the app falls
# back to its prepared answers. The assistant answers from on-device logic and
# labels itself "Answers computed on-device"; news digests and article summaries
# show their seeded text and say "no model call ran". Nothing breaks or looks
# broken — the app is built to be honest about which path produced an answer.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-REPLACE-ME


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Client-side. Safe to expose — these are bundled into the app.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the app sends assistant, digest, summary and scan requests. This is a
# public endpoint, not a secret: it holds no key, and the key it uses lives in
# the server environment above.
#
# Point it at your own deployment of `api/assistant.ts`, or at the hosted one:
#     https://collectee.vercel.app/api/assistant
#
# WITHOUT IT: identical to having no Anthropic key — every AI surface uses its
# prepared fallback and says so. This is the default state of a fresh clone.
EXPO_PUBLIC_AI_PROXY_URL=

# Set to 1 to skip the first-run flow (sign-in, 4-step quiz, guided tour) and
# land straight on Home. Useful when you are iterating and do not want to walk
# through onboarding on every reload.
#
# Leave it unset the first time you open the app — the first-run flow is a real
# part of the product and worth seeing once.
#
# WITHOUT IT: the first-run flow runs, which is the intended behaviour.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SKIP_FIRST_RUN=
